=== 4b. BUG FOUND: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR override path inconsistency ===
Ran the hook script directly with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/tmp/tourist-spike-exp4-direct/config
(a scratch override dir), sending a synthetic PreToolUse payload matching the
documented Claude Code hook JSON schema on stdin. Expected the attribution
log/pre-snapshot dir to land INSIDE the override dir
(/tmp/tourist-spike-exp4-direct/config/tourist-attribution/), matching how
install()/isInstalled() treat CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (used directly, no dirname).
Actual: it landed as a SIBLING of the override dir instead
(/tmp/tourist-spike-exp4-direct/tourist-attribution/, one level up) --
confirmed by `find`, both in hooks/attribution-hook.mjs's CONFIG_BASE
constant and (identical logic, so identically affected)
src/adapters/hook-log-reader.ts's attributionDir(). Root cause: both compute
`path.dirname(process.env.CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)` when the override is set,
instead of using the override directly the way the non-override default
branch uses `path.join(os.homedir(), ".claude")` (home ITSELF joined with
".claude", not home's dirname). See spike/FINDINGS.md experiment 4 for the
concrete fix and impact.

